ught them here to America you know or  to the US and tried them in courts and  then detained them somewhere you know or  at that point if they were found guilty  imprisoned them and somewhere like the  Supermax in Colorado or our you know the  maximum-security prison in Terre Haute  Indiana that somehow they would escape  and be loose or somehow they'd be  allowed to be loose and that's you know  that's the farthest thing from the truth  yeah I mean that argument sort of  implies that we don't we can't really  trust the most secure prisons in the US  right people inside right if the  argument is we even if they're on  American soil in in the most secure of  all prisons those programs just aren't  good enough is what the argument sort of  implies isn't it well that in and that  our US Court system our federal court  system here in America is somehow sub  subpar compared to the military  tribunals that have failed to even try  20 detainees in 15 years I want to talk  a little bit you mentioned PTSD  generalized anxiety as a result of this  incident where you were attacked by a  detainee at Gitmo when I introduced you  I mentioned you're also an advocate for  plant-based health options and one of  those that many people may not have  heard of and I hope I'm pronouncing this  right is Krita kratom how does it  pronounced correctly you'll generally  hear it either kratom or kratom okay  they're not to pronounce what that is  and the controversy surrounding it right  now sure so so kratom kratom is uh is a  it's it's a leaf off a tree generally  grown in Southeast Asia and Indonesia  Borneo imported here into the u.s. up  until this past year for the most part  the FDA and DEA played kind of hands-off  and then the FDA came in and  and did kind of an import alert early in  2015 and they started having the  marshals and customs seized shipments  from you know from vendors and it was  already kind of difficult for the  vendors because then they had to you  know just the way